Z||000000||Taijiguy||05-17-2001||10:51 PM||||Geeze! I ordered poly bushings from one place last week. Today I find out they're back-ordered to that distributor for three more weeks. So I order them from Suspension Restoration. They were plenty responsive, shipped them same day. Then I get a memo from Fed Ex, that includes this:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>Shipped Date.................:  5/17/2001<BR>Estimated Delivery Date......:  5/23/2001<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>6 friggin days for delivery? Cripes, are they walking here with my parts or what? <BR>Sheesh! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.core.com/~taijiguy/simpsons.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-17-2001||10:56 PM||||Hehe, funny picture.<P>Maybe they just know that you really <I>really</I> want the bushings so they are going to make you wait for them, and see if you want them as much as you think!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I know how things go with back orders.  I orderd some car wax about 5 weeks ago from the Ace Hardware where I work.  And every week I look on the order report and see that the item is backordered, and the shipment is supposed to come in within about 3 days.  Well, that shipment date keeps getting pushed back, and I am getting annoyed!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
