Z||000006||DXR_DAD||05-18-2001||01:16 AM||||Joe, You don't need any wax!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Your car looks just fine<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||10
Z||000007||pontiacs4me||05-18-2001||01:22 AM||||Dont wax a fresh paint job.  It will create a barrier on top of the clear coat, and will trap solvents that need to escape for the curing process.  It can take up to one year for a paintjob to fully cure, up to 4 years for a lacquer job to cure.  I wouldnt wax it until next summer.  Use a hand polish, it will wash off within 2 washes, make the paint look awesome, and it wont trap any solvents.<P>BTW, that is a new paint job isnt it?||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||05-18-2001||07:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B> But African Swallows are not migratory.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Maybe it was by European Swallow<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula||05-18-2001||09:16 AM||||Joe, your car loks awesome... I dont think I told you yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I wish I would have painted mine that color sometimes.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroJoe||05-18-2001||09:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pontiacs4me:<BR><B>BTW, that is a new paint job isnt it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, it is a new paint job, and yes, right now it is waxed.  I am not worring about the paint curing, becuase neither I nor my dad are happy with the way it came out.  It looks great in the pic, yes, but up close I'm embarrassed.  There was a little too much dust in the base coat, so we lightly sanded it out with 1500 before the clear.  But, what happened, was when we sanded the dust out, it pulled out little tiny pieces of the base, so the primer showed through.  Now, in some areas, I have little tiny white specks all over.  If I had used tinted primer, this might have been avoided.  Also, if I had a downdraft booth, but <I>that</I> will never happen.<P>Anyway, we're going to repaint it again sometime towards the end of the summer, or at earliest when we get this 67 Camaro SS restored and painted (for a friend).<P>Other than that, I still have to rub out the clear, because the compound we were using wasnt tough enough to get all the scratches from the 800 and 1500 out, so in direct sunlight I about hurl becuase it looks so shoddy.  Hopefully I can get it looking better before the Michigan Fiero Club show.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000011||84Bill||05-18-2001||10:58 AM||||Originally posted by FieroJoe:<P>Joe did you wet the floor and walls down before you painted it?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000012||Ken Wittlief||05-18-2001||11:09 AM||||you can make a respectable booth with plastic drop cloth, some 2 x 0.5" framing wood, a staple gun, a window fan, and a furnace air filter.<P>  dust is everywhere. If you dont have the car in filtered airspace, your gonna get dust in the paint.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tina||05-18-2001||10:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Taijiguy:<BR><B>Geeze! I ordered poly bushings from one place last week. Today I find out they're back-ordered to that distributor for three more weeks.  <IMG SRC="http://members.core.com/~taijiguy/simpsons.gif">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Same thing happend to me,backordered.<BR>But never bothered letting me know about it.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Ended up ordering the parts from the Fiero-Store,and of course got the part#'s mixed up.<P>What next?<BR>At this rate, I should have the Fiero back on the road by 2002.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tina||05-18-2001||10:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tina:<BR><B> Same thing happend to me,backordered.<BR>But never bothered letting me know about it.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Ended up ordering the parts from the Fiero-Store,and of course I got the part#'s mixed up.<P>What next?<BR>At this rate, I should have the Fiero back on the road by 2002.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||FieroJoe||05-18-2001||10:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84Bill:<BR><B>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<P>Joe did you wet the floor and walls down before you painted it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, we always do for every car we paint.  I vacuumed the walls and covered up most of our machinery and cabinets in our shop.  We did have our air mover fan (big 30" fan blows air outside) on while painting, so that could have stirred up a bunch.<P>I have had second thoughts about repainting it again.  After all, it <I>is</I> my daily driver, not a concours car, and if I can get the clear coat rubbed out, I think I'll be happy.  After all, it only cost me $350 in materials, and I bet no shop around my area can touch that for how good it looks, and how well it will hold up (no maaco job here!)<P>I will have to see what my dad thinks about making a booth like that, sounds pretty simple.  Maybe we can try it before we paint the camaro. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Taijiguy||05-19-2001||08:34 PM||||Tina:<BR>The first place didn't notify me either. (Phil's) I called two days after I placed the order, since I didn't receive an email notice of the order. They said out of stock until the next Tuesday, then I called again after still not receiving any notice. Thats when they let me know it was back ordered. Suspension Restoration was cheaper than the Fiero Store. ||||reg||1
